{
 "notes": [
  "Matched the concept facade by placing the two-car porch on the right and the tall glazed drawing room with front lawn on the left, unified under the cantilevered upper concrete frame and timber louver screen.",
  "The parents' bedroom is positioned quietly at the rear of the ground floor with its own attached bath, while the open kitchen connects directly to the central TV lounge and adjacent dirty kitchen, both looking onto the rear service space.",
  "The dog-leg stair along the left party wall uses a 15 ft hall with a 4 ft landing at the south (-y) end, keeping circulation compact and centralized.",
  "Upstairs, three bedrooms (4 total in the house), a family lounge, and a dedicated prayer room are arranged around the central core, with wet areas stacked over the ground-floor bath and kitchens.",
  "Both lounges extend across to the 5 ft eastern side setback to receive abundant natural daylight and ventilation."
 ],
